<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Subhas Chandra Bose</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1897–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Netaji</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Subhas Chandra Bose was an Indian nationalist leader, twice president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a>. Seeking foreign help against British rule, he went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and then Japanese-held Asia, where in 1943 he proclaimed the Provisional Government of Free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> (Azad Hind) and led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-army">Indian National Army</a>. He died after a plane crash in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/subhas-chandra-bose.jpg" alt="Subhas Chandra Bose" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown (Netaji Research Bureau, Calcutta) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Subhas_Chandra_Bose_NRB.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
